{"changes":["Standard 1.7 (new): the optional content field `checks` — an array of `{command, scope}` objects. `command` is a shell command run at the repository root (non-zero exit is a blocking violation); `scope` is the same repo-relative forward-slash glob grammar as `appliesTo`. Malformed declarations are an R0 structural violation, the same class as a malformed `appliesTo`. An Artifact that declares no checks is checklist-only. (specification/exchange.md, concepts.md, versioning.md; EKA/README/CHANGELOG bumped.)","eka-core v1.13.0: `pathglob.InterpretChecks` + `pathglob.Check`; `contexts.(*Engine).DeclaredChecks(projectID, sourceRepo)` (repository-scoped, deterministic order, malformed → error), mirroring the M1 `UnitsForPath`/`UnmatchedScopes` doctrine; `conformance.checkChecks` (R0, wired into Validate + ValidateCKO). SpecificationVersion 1.6 → 1.7; 1.6 added to the accepted import set.","eka-cli v1.26.0: `eka verify` executes declared checks after the built-in set; each result is `declared:\u003ccanonicalForm\u003e` with Constraint = the declaring Artifact's canonical id; a non-zero exit blocks (not defeatable except by --force). New built-in check `standard-checks` reports every constraint Artifact as `enforced: \u003cn\u003e check(s)` or `checklist-only` (warning, never blocks). An empty/absent scope matches nothing, so a declared check runs only without a --changed filter.","eka-mcp v1.16.0: pins eka-core v1.13.0 (grouped retrieval surface, sto:retrieval-surface-budget)."],"role":"implementation","summary":"M3b (sto:standard-check-declarations) is complete. A constraint Artifact can now declare the checks that verify it — the machine-answerable form of 'how is this enforced' — and `eka verify` runs them, resolving each to the constraint id of the declaring Artifact. A standard with no checks is reported checklist-only, never treated as enforced. Shipped as EKA Standard 1.7 with the cascade across core, cli and mcp.","tests":["eka-cli: `TestVerifyDeclaredCheckNonVacuity` proves both directions on a git fixture — the declaration catches the change, and removing it makes the same change pass; `TestVerifyStandardChecksChecklistOnly` proves an Artifact with no checks is reported checklist-only and never blocks. `go test ./cmd/ -count=1` green; `anvil pipeline ci` PASS.","eka-core: contexts/conformance/exchange/pathglob suites green; `./scripts/coverage-gate.sh` exit 0; ci PASS; release v1.13.0.","eka-standard: release v1.7 published (docs-only).","Real declaration (AC4 'at least one standard in this repository declares a real check'): std:development-rules:3 now declares {command: 'go vet ./cmd/...', scope: ['cmd/**']}; `eka verify` reports `[PASS] declared:eka/std:development-rules:3` and `standard-checks` reports `eka/std:development-rules:3: enforced: 1 check(s)`; the other artifacts report checklist-only."]}